## 4. Port mapping

### `Tool` (`tool.rb` → `tool.py`)

Ruby: `Struct.new(:name, :description, :parameters, :block)` with a custom `to_s`.

| Ruby | Python |
|------|--------|
| `Struct.new(:name, :description, :parameters, :block)` | `@dataclass` with the same four fields in the same positional order |
| `parameters` is a hash such as `{ direction: { type: "string", description: "..." } }` | `dict[str, dict]` keyed by parameter name |
| `block` is a lambda (`->(direction) { ... }`) | `Callable`, passed as the fourth argument |
| `to_s`: `#<Tool name=… description=<first 41 chars> params=[:direction]>` | `__str__` returning the same text (see gotchas 1, 3, 4) |

### `Message` (`message.rb` → `message.py`)

Ruby: `Struct.new(:role, :content, :tool_use_id)` with a custom `to_s`.

| Ruby | Python |
|------|--------|
| `Struct.new(:role, :content, :tool_use_id)` | `@dataclass` with `role`, `content`, `tool_use_id=None` |
| `role` is a symbol (`:user`, `:assistant`, `:tool_result`) | See Q4 (string versus `Enum`) |
| `to_s`: `#<Message role=user [id] content=<first 61 chars>...>` | `__str__` with the same text. The ` [id]` tag appears only when `tool_use_id` is set. |

### `Context` (`context.rb` → `context.py`)

| Ruby | Python |
|------|--------|
| `initialize(task:, system: nil)` | `__init__(self, *, task, system=None)`, keyword-only like the Ruby call |
| `attr_reader :task, :system, :messages, :tools` | read-only `@property`s over `_task`, `_system`, `_messages`, `_tools` |
| `@messages = []`, `@tools = {}` | `list` and `dict` |
| `register_tool(tool)` stores `@tools[tool.name] = tool` | same; re-registering a name replaces the old tool |
| `add_message(role, content, tool_use_id: nil)` | `add_message(self, role, content, *, tool_use_id=None)` |
| `tool_count`, `turn_count` | follow Q5 (properties recommended) |
| `to_s`: `#<Context task=player turns=2 tools=1>` | `__str__`. `task&.task_name` becomes `task.task_name if task is not None else ""`. |

`task` is the task **class** (`Player`), not an instance. Tasks are stateless classmethod holders, as in 00.

